@page "/"
@using System.Globalization
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@implements IAsyncDisposable

<PageTitle>Alectrone Calendar &middot; Scheduling for Teams</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Alectrone Calendar puts team scheduling, public booking pages, and an AI assistant on one calendar. Seven views, field-level encryption, role-scoped permissions." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Alectrone Calendar &middot; Scheduling for Teams" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Team scheduling, public booking pages, and an AI assistant on one calendar." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Alectrone Calendar" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
</HeadContent>

@*
    WASM DEMO of the Alectrone.Calendar.Web landing page. Markup, scoped CSS
    (Home.razor.css) and the scene engine (wwwroot/js/landing-scenes.js) are
    generated from Components/Pages/LandingPage.razor in that host by
    e2e/calendar/scripts/port-landing-to-demo.mjs. DO NOT hand-edit this file:
    run the porter instead, or the next port will overwrite you, and a
    hand-port is how this demo previously fell ten hours behind and lost the
    autoplay engine, the Accounts scene and the booking pin without anyone
    noticing.

    Two deliberate removals for this demo, everything else verbatim:
      - No auth chrome. There is no server behind this deploy, so every
        /Account/* call to action and footer link would 404. The header keeps
        its .landing__auth-actions container (it carries margin-left:auto and
        hosts the mobile nav toggle) but holds no buttons.
      - No pricing. No plan catalog ships here and the page quotes no price,
        so the Pricing nav item, the #pricing scene, its chapter-rail stop and
        the footer link are all absent.
    Where a removed call to action carried a scene's visual weight, the button
    is KEPT and repointed at the in-page chapter it introduces, so every
    scene's composition and motion choreography are unchanged.

    Motion is progressive enhancement: landing-scenes.js only flips state
    classes and publishes CSS custom properties; the scoped CSS performs every
    transition. The engine is imported from OnAfterRenderAsync below (the Web
    host uses a JS initializer instead, because "/" is static SSR there with no
    circuit to run interop from). The one contract that CANNOT hold on
    WebAssembly is the JavaScript-disabled pose - nothing renders at all
    without the runtime - so the base (no .has-motion) CSS survives purely as
    the reduced-motion and pre-arm pose.

    Content rule: every claim on this page is verifiable in this repository.
    Proof numbers are counted in code (SchedulerView, AccessManager
    permissions, AES-GCM, the AI provider chain). No adoption statistics until
    they are measured.
*@

<div id="calendar-landing" class="landing">

    @* ── Top Nav (T11: quiet chrome, elevation flips with hysteresis).
         Mobile: base CSS keeps the anchors as an in-flow second row (works
         with JS off and under reduced motion); the engine upgrades it to a
         toggle-driven panel (.nav-open) when motion is armed. ── *@
    <header class="landing__header">
        <div class="landing__header-inner">
            <a href="/" class="landing__brand">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="32" height="32" aria-hidden="true">
                    <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="15" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)" opacity="0.15"/>
                    <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="10" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)" opacity="0.3"/>
                    <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="5"  fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)"/>
                </svg>
                <span>Alectrone Calendar</span>
            </a>

            <nav id="landing-nav" class="landing__nav" aria-label="Marketing navigation">
                @* In-page chapters only: this deploy has no other route and no
                   sign-in endpoint, so every item lands on a scene that exists. *@
                <a href="#schedule">Product</a>
                <a href="#views">Views</a>
                <a href="#booking">Booking</a>
                <a href="#colorways">Colorways</a>
            </nav>

            <div class="landing__auth-actions">
                @* The auth buttons are gone in the demo; the container stays because
                   it carries margin-left:auto (it keeps the nav left-aligned after
                   the brand) and it hosts the mobile nav toggle. *@
                <button type="button" class="landing__nav-toggle" aria-label="Menu"
                        aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="landing-nav">
                    <span class="landing__nav-toggle-bar"></span>
                    <span class="landing__nav-toggle-bar"></span>
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    @* ── Chapter spine (T18): appears after the hero, tracks the chapter in view ── *@
    <nav class="landing-rail" aria-label="Page chapters">
        <div class="landing-rail__inner">
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="schedule"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">Schedule</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="views"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">Views</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="booking"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">Booking</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="colorways"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">Colorways</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="modes"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">Accounts</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="ai"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">AI</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="landing-rail__link" data-rail="proof"><span class="landing-rail__dot"></span><span class="landing-rail__label">Proof</span></button>
        </div>
    </nav>

    @* ══ Scene 1 · Hook: a T15-style overture on a sticky runway. Entrance
         choreography and pointer parallax (T1), then a scrubbed film on
         --exit: the supporting copy recedes, the title shrinks and rises
         away, and the statement grows from a subtitle into the display
         line, fills, holds, and hands focus to its second line before the
         stage departs (T14). Scrolling up replays it in reverse. Base,
         mobile, and reduced motion keep the single-viewport composition. ══ *@
    <section class="landing-hero" data-hero data-autoplay="4500" data-scene>
      <div class="landing-hero__stage">
        <div class="landing-hero__backdrop" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="landing-aurora landing-aurora--violet" data-depth="90"></span>
            <span class="landing-aurora landing-aurora--indigo" data-depth="55"></span>
            <span class="landing-aurora landing-aurora--orchid" data-depth="30"></span>
            <span class="landing-hero__gridsheet" data-depth="14"></span>
        </div>

        @* Editorial split: the copy holds the left column and the crafted week
           calendar the right. The copy's scroll overture is transform-driven,
           so it plays here on the left exactly as it did centred (the user's
           requirement); the two columns never overlap, so no scrim is needed. *@
        <div class="landing-hero__layout">
            <div class="landing-hero__inner">
                <p class="landing-eyebrow landing-hero__e1">Alectrone Calendar</p>
                <h1 class="landing-hero__title landing-hero__e2">
                    Own the <span class="landing-accent">week.</span>
                </h1>
                @* The chapter statement lives under the title: a subtitle at
                   rest, it grows into the display line as the visitor scrolls
                   (two-beat fill + line handoff ride the same scrub). *@
                <h2 class="landing-hero__statement landing-hero__e2b">
                    <span class="landing-hero__statement-line landing-hero__statement-line--1">Stop arranging time.</span>
                    <span class="landing-hero__statement-line landing-hero__statement-line--2">Start directing it.</span>
                </h2>
                <p class="landing-hero__lede landing-hero__e3">
                    Calendar, bookings, and availability: one place where your
                    team's time comes together. Seven ways to see the week, one
                    link to get booked, and an assistant that turns plain words
                    into events.
                </p>
                @* The two account shapes, named on the first screen and linked to
                   the chapter that defines them, so a visitor never has to scroll
                   to learn which one they are. It sits between the lede and the
                   controls: the visitor knows which shape they are before they
                   are asked to choose a button. *@
                <a href="#modes" class="landing-hero__modes landing-hero__e4">
                    <b>Personal</b> for your own calendar,
                    <b>Workspace</b> when it is a team
                </a>
                <div class="landing-hero__cta-row landing-hero__e4b">
                    <a href="#schedule" class="landing__btn landing__btn--primary landing__btn--lg">
                        See it move
                    </a>
                    <a href="#views" class="landing__btn landing__btn--outline landing__btn--lg">
                        Every view
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            @* Concept A, elevated: the week orbits a PRECISE TIME DIAL at the
               centre, in true perspective, over deep-space atmosphere. The dial
               is watch-grade linework (fine ticks, real-time hands, one iris
               accent, an iris sweep hand) rather than a glowing orb; each day
               swells and sharpens as it sweeps to the near edge of the tilted
               plane and recedes small and soft around the far side. The wrapper
               owns perspective + the JS parallax transform; the inner plane owns
               the rake, entrance, and --exit recede. Hidden from assistive tech. *@
            <div class="landing-hero__sun" data-depth="30" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="landing-hsun">
                    <span class="landing-hsun__space"></span>
                    <span class="landing-hsun__nebula"></span>
                    <span class="landing-hsun__corona"></span>
                    <span class="landing-hsun__path landing-hsun__path--outer"></span>
                    <span class="landing-hsun__path landing-hsun__path--inner"></span>
                    @* The orbit is a REAL dated week, not seven decorative dots:
                       each seat carries its weekday and its own date, and one of
                       them is today. Every seat renders the "Today" callout in
                       markup and CSS shows it only under --on, so the engine can
                       move today to the visitor's own day by flipping one class
                       (localizeToday in landing-scenes.js) without inserting or
                       moving a node. *@
                    <div class="landing-hsun__orbit" data-hsun-orbit>
                        @{
                            var sunDays = new[] { "Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun" };
                            var sunToday = ((int)_today.DayOfWeek + 6) % 7;
                            var sunStep = 360.0 / 7.0;
                        }
                        @* Today's tether: a hairline radius from the dial's edge out
                           to today's seat. It rides inside the spinning group, so it
                           stays locked to that seat, and it brightens with the seat
                           as the pair sweeps the near arc. The dial points at today. *@
                        <span class="landing-hsun__tether" data-hsun-tether
                              style="--a:@((sunToday * sunStep).ToString("0.###", Inv))deg;--i:@sunToday"></span>
                        @for (var i = 0; i < 7; i++)
                        {
                            var a = (i * sunStep).ToString("0.###", Inv);
                            var c = _dotPalette[i % _dotPalette.Length];
                            <span class="landing-hsun__day@(i == sunToday ? " landing-hsun__day--on" : null)"
                                  data-hsun-day="@i" style="--a:@(a)deg;--i:@i;--c:@c">
                                <span class="landing-hsun__body">
                                    <span class="landing-hsun__depth">
                                        <span class="landing-hsun__tag">Today</span>
                                        <span class="landing-hsun__dot"></span>
                                        <span class="landing-hsun__label">@sunDays[i]</span>
                                        <span class="landing-hsun__date" data-hsun-date>@_weekDays[i].Day</span>
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-hsun__core">
                        <span class="landing-hsun__dial">
                            <svg class="landing-hsun__clock" viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                                @* Minute ticks with brighter hour ticks; 12 o'clock is the one iris accent. *@
                                @for (var m = 0; m < 60; m++)
                                {
                                    var isHour = m % 5 == 0;
                                    var tang = (m * 6).ToString(Inv);
                                    var y2 = isHour ? "15" : "11.5";
                                    var stroke = m == 0
                                        ? "hsl(268, 70%, 66%)"
                                        : (isHour ? "hsla(268, 18%, 90%, 0.5)" : "hsla(268, 14%, 84%, 0.22)");
                                    var sw = isHour ? "1.1" : "0.7";
                                    <line x1="60" y1="9" x2="60" y2="@y2" transform="rotate(@tang 60 60)" stroke="@stroke" stroke-width="@sw" stroke-linecap="round" />
                                }
                                @* Hands at the real current time (server clock; decorative). *@
                                <line x1="60" y1="62.5" x2="60" y2="35" transform="rotate(@_clockHour 60 60)" stroke="hsla(268, 12%, 92%, 0.9)" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                                <line x1="60" y1="63.5" x2="60" y2="21" transform="rotate(@_clockMin 60 60)" stroke="hsla(268, 10%, 96%, 0.96)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" />
                                <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="2.6" fill="hsl(268, 24%, 90%)" />
                                <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="1.1" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 52%)" />
                            </svg>
                        </span>
                        <span class="landing-hsun__now"></span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="landing-hero__cue landing-hero__e5" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="landing-hero__cue-dot"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    @* ══ Scene 3 · SCHEDULE: sticky-runway pose morph (T12). Pose 1: your
         solo week as an inset rounded card. One flick: the SAME calendar
         swells to full bleed and the team layer fades in. Widening the frame
         IS the pitch: your calendar grows into the team's canvas. The flip
         commits at 60% progress going down, 20% going up; the gap between
         them is the hysteresis dead zone. ══ *@
    <section id="schedule" class="landing-week" data-pose data-autoplay="4000" data-chapter="schedule" aria-label="Team scheduling">
        <div class="landing-week__stage">
            <div class="landing-week__dawn" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="landing-week__media" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="landing-week__app">
                    <div class="landing-week__appbar">
                        <span class="landing-week__mark">
                            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="16" height="16">
                                <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="15" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)" opacity="0.15"/>
                                <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="10" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)" opacity="0.3"/>
                                <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="5"  fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)"/>
                            </svg>
                        </span>
                        <span class="landing-week__month">@_monthLabel</span>
                        <span class="landing-week__avatars">
                            <span class="landing-week__avatar" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%)">MC</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__avatar" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%)">JR</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__avatar" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%)">AL</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__avatar landing-week__avatar--more">+3</span>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="landing-week__grid">
                        <span class="landing-week__now" style="--t:36"></span>
                        <div class="landing-week__col">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Mon</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%);--t:16;--h:22">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Design review</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">9:00 - 10:30</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%);--t:52;--h:16">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Standup</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">13:00 · 15 min</span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="landing-week__col">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Tue</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%);--t:8;--h:26">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Deep work</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">8:00 - 11:00</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-meta">Focus block</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%);--t:44;--h:28">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Sprint planning</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">11:30 - 13:00</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-people">
                                    <span style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%)"></span>
                                    <span style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%)"></span>
                                    <span style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%)"></span>
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="landing-week__col">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Wed</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%);--t:30;--h:16">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">1:1 with Sam</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">10:30</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%);--t:56;--h:22">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Design crit</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">14:30 - 15:30</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-meta">Room 4</span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="landing-week__col">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Thu</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%);--t:12;--h:20">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Roadmap</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">9:00 - 10:00</span>
                            </span>
                            @* The overlap arrives with the team layer: two meetings colliding
                               the way real calendars do, side by side, not stacked. *@
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team landing-week__ev--nudge" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%);--t:22;--h:14">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Debrief</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team landing-week__ev--pulse" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%);--t:40;--h:30">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Customer demo</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">13:00 - 14:30</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-meta">Video call</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-people">
                                    <span style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%)"></span>
                                    <span style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%)"></span>
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="landing-week__col">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Fri</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%);--t:20;--h:18">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Retro</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">10:00 - 11:00</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%);--t:46;--h:14">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Office hours</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">14:00 - 15:00</span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="landing-week__col landing-week__col--wknd">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Sat</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="landing-week__col landing-week__col--wknd">
                            <span class="landing-week__day">Sun</span>
                            <span class="landing-week__ev landing-week__ev--team" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%);--t:24;--h:14">
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-title">Brunch</span>
                                <span class="landing-week__ev-time">11:00</span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                @* T23 lit stage: two symmetric overhead beams (a single beam
                   over full bleed reads as a streak; the pair reads as a rig)
                   and a theater vignette. Scoped to the media box, clipped by
                   the stage's overflow, tinted by the app's colorway cycle. *@
                <div class="landing-week__rig" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="landing-week__beam landing-week__beam--l"></span>
                    <span class="landing-week__beam landing-week__beam--r"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-week__vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="landing-week__band">
                <div class="landing-week__captions">
                    @* The two poses ARE the two account shapes, so the eyebrows
                       name them: the words the visitor meets again on the
                       #modes rule. *@
                    <div class="landing-week__cap landing-week__cap--1">
                        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Personal</p>
                        <h2 class="landing-week__title">Your week, at a glance</h2>
                        <p class="landing-week__desc">Day, week, and month views with drag-and-drop. Fast, focused, yours.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="landing-week__cap landing-week__cap--2">
                        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Workspace</p>
                        <h2 class="landing-week__title">The whole team, on one canvas</h2>
                        <p class="landing-week__desc">Shared calendars, role-based access, and live availability across your entire organization.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ══ Scene 4 · VIEWS: the horizontal film. A true overflow-x scroller:
         side wheel, vertical wheel over the strip, Shift+wheel, arrow keys,
         touch, and the visible scrollbar all drive it (wheel mapping lives
         in landing-scenes.js with boundary release, so the page is never
         trapped). With JS off or reduced motion it is a plain native
         scroller. Mocks are decorative; the seven views are real: the
         SchedulerView enum this app renders. ══ *@
    <section id="views" class="landing-views" data-scene data-pin data-autoplay="7000" data-chapter="views" aria-label="Calendar views">
      <div class="landing-views__stage">
        <header class="landing-views__head">
            <p class="landing-eyebrow">The views</p>
            <h2 class="landing-views__title">One calendar, many ways to read it</h2>
            <p class="landing-views__desc">
                Day for the next hour, week for the shape of things, month for
                the promises you made. Every view here ships in the scheduler
                today.
            </p>
        </header>

        <div class="landing-views__stripwrap">
            <div class="landing-views__strip" data-hstrip tabindex="0" role="region"
                 aria-label="Calendar view gallery, scrolls horizontally">
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--day" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="lv-hd">
                            <span class="lv-hd__dow" data-td="day-dow">@_dayDow</span>
                            <span class="lv-hd__num" data-td="day-num">@_dayNum</span>
                            <span class="lv-hd__mon" data-td="day-mon">@_dayMon</span>
                            <span class="lv-hd__tag">Today</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="lv-allday">
                            <span class="lv-allday__tag">All day</span>
                            <span class="lv-allday__chip" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%)">Team offsite</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="lv-day__body">
                            <span class="lv-day__gutter"><b>08</b><b>10</b><b>12</b><b>14</b><b>16</b><b>18</b></span>
                            <span class="lv-day__track">
                                <span class="lv-ev" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%);--t:6;--h:12"><b class="lv-ev__t">Design review</b><i class="lv-ev__m">09:00 - 09:45</i></span>
                                <span class="lv-ev" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%);--t:26;--h:26"><b class="lv-ev__t">Deep work</b><i class="lv-ev__m">10:30 - 12:00 · Focus</i></span>
                                <span class="lv-ev" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%);--t:60;--h:11"><b class="lv-ev__t">Standup</b><i class="lv-ev__m">14:00</i></span>
                                <span class="lv-ev" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%);--t:78;--h:14"><b class="lv-ev__t">1:1 with Sam</b><i class="lv-ev__m">16:00 - 16:30</i></span>
                                <span class="lv-day__now" data-td-nowline style="--t:@_nowPct"></span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Day</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">This hour, at full size.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--week" aria-hidden="true">
                        @for (var i = 0; i < 7; i++)
                        {
                            var d = _weekDays[i];
                            <span class="lv-col @(i >= 5 ? "lv-col--wknd" : null) @(d == _today ? "lv-col--today" : null)" data-td-col="@i">
                                <span class="lv-colhd"><b class="lv-colhd__d" data-td-coldow>@d.ToString("ddd", Inv)</b><i class="lv-colhd__n" data-td-colday>@d.Day</i></span>
                                <span class="lv-col__body">
                                    <span class="lv-col__now" data-td-nowline style="--t:@_nowPct"></span>
                                    @foreach (var b in _weekBlocks[i])
                                    {
                                        <span class="lv-blk" style="--c:@b.C;--t:@b.T;--h:@b.H">
                                            <b class="lv-blk__t">@b.Name</b>
                                            @if (b.Time is not null)
                                            {
                                                <i class="lv-blk__m">@b.Time</i>
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Week</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">The default. The whole shape of the week in one look.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--wweek" aria-hidden="true">
                        @for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++)
                        {
                            var d = _weekDays[i];
                            <span class="lv-col @(d == _today ? "lv-col--today" : null)" data-td-col="@i">
                                <span class="lv-colhd"><b class="lv-colhd__d" data-td-coldow>@d.ToString("ddd", Inv)</b><i class="lv-colhd__n" data-td-colday>@d.Day</i></span>
                                <span class="lv-col__body">
                                    <span class="lv-col__now" data-td-nowline style="--t:@_nowPct"></span>
                                    @foreach (var b in _wweekBlocks[i])
                                    {
                                        <span class="lv-blk" style="--c:@b.C;--t:@b.T;--h:@b.H">
                                            <b class="lv-blk__t">@b.Name</b>
                                            @if (b.Time is not null)
                                            {
                                                <i class="lv-blk__m">@b.Time</i>
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Work week</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">Monday to Friday, weekends off the books.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--month" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="lv-hd"><span class="lv-hd__title" data-td="month-label">@_monthLabel</span></div>
                        <div class="lv-month__dow"><span>Mon</span><span>Tue</span><span>Wed</span><span>Thu</span><span>Fri</span><span>Sat</span><span>Sun</span></div>
                        <div class="lv-month__grid">
                            @for (var i = 0; i < 42; i++)
                            {
                                var d = _monthCells[i];
                                var outMonth = d.Month != _monthNumber;
                                var isToday = d == _today;
                                var ev = !outMonth && System.Array.IndexOf(_monthDotDays, d.Day) >= 0;
                                <span class="lv-cell @(outMonth ? "lv-cell--out" : null) @(isToday ? "lv-cell--today" : null) @(ev ? "lv-cell--ev" : null)" data-td-cell="@i" style="@(ev ? $"--c:{DotColor(d.Day)}" : null)"><i class="lv-cell__n" data-td-cellnum>@d.Day</i><s class="lv-cell__dot"></s></span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Month</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">Commitments at a distance.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--year" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="lv-hd"><span class="lv-hd__title" data-td="year">@_yearLabel</span></div>
                        <div class="lv-year__grid">
                            @for (var m = 0; m < 12; m++)
                            {
                                var shape = _yearMonths[m];
                                <span class="lv-mini @(m == _currentMonthIndex ? "lv-mini--now" : null)" data-td-mini="@m">
                                    <b class="lv-mini__name">@_monthAbbrevs[m]</b>
                                    <span class="lv-mini__grid">
                                        @for (var pad = 0; pad < shape.Lead; pad++)
                                        {
                                            <s class="lv-md lv-md--pad"></s>
                                        }
                                        @for (var day = 1; day <= shape.Days; day++)
                                        {
                                            var isToday = m == _currentMonthIndex && day == _todayDay;
                                            <s class="lv-md @(isToday ? "lv-md--today" : null)" data-td-yday="@day"></s>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Year</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">Twelve months on one screen, for the long game.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--agenda" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="lv-ag__group">
                            <span class="lv-ag__day" data-td-rel="0"><em class="lv-ag__rel" data-td-rellabel>@RelLabel(0)</em><i class="lv-ag__date" data-td-reldate>@RelDate(0)</i></span>
                            <span class="lv-ag__ev" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%)"><i class="lv-ag__t">09:00</i><b class="lv-ag__x">Design review</b><u class="lv-ag__m">Room 4</u></span>
                            <span class="lv-ag__ev" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%)"><i class="lv-ag__t">13:00</i><b class="lv-ag__x">Standup</b><u class="lv-ag__m">15 min</u></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="lv-ag__group">
                            <span class="lv-ag__day" data-td-rel="1"><em class="lv-ag__rel" data-td-rellabel>@RelLabel(1)</em><i class="lv-ag__date" data-td-reldate>@RelDate(1)</i></span>
                            <span class="lv-ag__ev" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%)"><i class="lv-ag__t">10:00</i><b class="lv-ag__x">Sprint planning</b><u class="lv-ag__m">90 min</u></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="lv-ag__group">
                            <span class="lv-ag__day" data-td-rel="2"><em class="lv-ag__rel" data-td-rellabel>@RelLabel(2)</em><i class="lv-ag__date" data-td-reldate>@RelDate(2)</i></span>
                            <span class="lv-ag__ev" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%)"><i class="lv-ag__t">15:30</i><b class="lv-ag__x">Design crit</b><u class="lv-ag__m">Studio</u></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Agenda</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">A straight list of what is next.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-views__panel">
                    <div class="landing-views__mock lv--tline" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="lv-hd">
                            <span class="lv-hd__title" data-td="tl-date">@_tlDate</span>
                            <span class="lv-tline__axis"><i>9a</i><i>11a</i><i>1p</i><i>3p</i><i>5p</i></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="lv-tline__lanes">
                            <span class="lv-lane"><em class="lv-lane__label">Room A</em><span class="lv-lane__track"><span class="lv-tline__now" data-td-tlnow style="--x:@_tlNowPct"></span><span class="lv-bar" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%);--l:6;--w:30">Ethics</span><span class="lv-bar" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%);--l:52;--w:24">Redox</span></span></span>
                            <span class="lv-lane"><em class="lv-lane__label">Room B</em><span class="lv-lane__track"><span class="lv-tline__now" data-td-tlnow style="--x:@_tlNowPct"></span><span class="lv-bar" style="--c:hsl(160, 60%, 45%);--l:22;--w:40">Calculus</span></span></span>
                            <span class="lv-lane"><em class="lv-lane__label">Studio</em><span class="lv-lane__track"><span class="lv-tline__now" data-td-tlnow style="--x:@_tlNowPct"></span><span class="lv-bar" style="--c:hsl(38, 80%, 55%);--l:12;--w:18">Ballet</span><span class="lv-bar" style="--c:hsl(268, 60%, 58%);--l:66;--w:26">Fossils</span></span></span>
                            <span class="lv-lane"><em class="lv-lane__label">Lab B</em><span class="lv-lane__track"><span class="lv-tline__now" data-td-tlnow style="--x:@_tlNowPct"></span><span class="lv-bar" style="--c:hsl(220, 70%, 58%);--l:34;--w:30">Optics</span></span></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="landing-views__name">Timeline</span>
                    <span class="landing-views__note">Rooms, people, and resources side by side.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <span class="landing-views__fade landing-views__fade--l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="landing-views__fade landing-views__fade--r" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>

        <p class="landing-views__hint">Tilt your wheel, hold Shift, or just scroll: the strip follows.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    @* ══ Scene 5 · BOOKING: trip-wire performance (T3). The moment the scene
         is on stage, the booking page demos itself: slots pop in, one gets
         picked, the confirmation lands. Scroll back up past it and return:
         it performs again, identically. ══ *@
    <section id="booking" class="landing-booking" data-scene data-pin data-autoplay="3500" data-chapter="booking" aria-label="Booking pages">
        <div class="landing-booking__pin">
        <div class="landing-booking__grid">
            <div class="landing-booking__copy">
                <p class="landing-eyebrow">Booking pages</p>
                @* Two lines, two beats. The runway fills them in reading order
                   (the hero statement's grammar): line one while the Focus
                   picker holds, line two across the turn, so the sentence
                   finishes at the moment the card lands on the month. *@
                <h2 class="landing-booking__title">
                    <span class="landing-booking__title-line landing-booking__title-line--1">Share one link.</span>
                    <span class="landing-booking__title-line landing-booking__title-line--2">Get booked.</span>
                </h2>
                <p class="landing-booking__desc">
                    Publish your availability as a public booking page. Visitors
                    pick from the slots that are still free, and the booking
                    lands straight on your calendar.
                </p>
                @* --i indexes each point into the runway: they light one after
                   another as the scroll passes them, ahead of the flip. *@
                <ul class="landing-booking__points">
                    <li style="--i:0">One /book link for every page you publish</li>
                    <li style="--i:1">Taken slots stay taken: double bookings are blocked</li>
                    <li style="--i:2">Every booking tracked and managed in one place</li>
                </ul>
                <a href="#colorways" class="landing__btn landing__btn--primary">Keep going</a>
            </div>

            <div class="landing-booking__stagebox" data-viewfocus aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="landing-booking__card">
                    <div class="landing-booking__head">
                        <span class="landing-booking__who">Book time with Maya Chen</span>
                        <span class="landing-booking__meta">Product demo · 30 min · Video call</span>
                    </div>

                    @* Two views, one page. The scene PINS: scroll scrubs the card
                       from the compact Focus picker to the month Calendar, holds on
                       Calendar, then releases (engine publishes --p on the pin). *@
                    <div class="landing-booking__switch">
                        <span class="landing-booking__switch-thumb"></span>
                        <span class="landing-booking__switch-label">Focus</span>
                        <span class="landing-booking__switch-label">Calendar</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="landing-booking__flipwrap">
                        <div class="landing-booking__flip">
                            <div class="landing-booking__face landing-booking__face--front">
                                <span class="landing-booking__daylabel">@_bookingDayLabel</span>
                                <div class="landing-booking__slots">
                                    <span class="landing-booking__slot">09:00</span>
                                    <span class="landing-booking__slot landing-booking__slot--picked">10:30</span>
                                    <span class="landing-booking__slot">11:30</span>
                                    <span class="landing-booking__slot">13:00</span>
                                    <span class="landing-booking__slot">14:30</span>
                                    <span class="landing-booking__slot">16:00</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="landing-booking__face landing-booking__face--back" aria-hidden="true">
                                <span class="landing-booking__cal-month">August 2026</span>
                                <div class="landing-booking__cal-grid">
                                    @foreach (var d in new[] { "M", "T", "W", "T", "F", "S", "S" })
                                    {
                                        <span class="landing-booking__cal-dow">@d</span>
                                    }
                                    @* Aug 1 2026 is a Saturday: 5 Monday-first leading blanks. *@
                                    @for (var b = 0; b < 5; b++)
                                    {
                                        <span class="landing-booking__cal-pad"></span>
                                    }
                                    @for (var day = 1; day <= 31; day++)
                                    {
                                        var sel = day == 4;
                                        var dot = day is 8 or 12 or 19 or 26;
                                        <span class="landing-booking__cal-day @(sel ? "landing-booking__cal-day--sel" : "") @(dot ? "landing-booking__cal-day--dot" : "")">@day</span>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="landing-booking__toast">
                        <span class="landing-booking__toast-check">
                            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                        </span>
                        Confirmed · Tuesday 10:30 · on your calendar
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ══ Scene 6 · COLORWAYS: the theater (T20) hosting the colorway lab
         (T21). A pinned runway with three acts: scroll commits a colorway
         inside narrow bands separated by dead zones (the T12 hysteresis
         generalized), the swatch buttons pin a choice, and the pin
         releases only when scroll commits a different act. One custom
         property (--cw) re-themes every surface; that is the pitch, and
         it is true of the token engine this platform ships. ══ *@
    <section id="colorways" class="landing-cw" data-pin data-cwlab data-autoplay="8000" data-chapter="colorways" aria-label="Colorways">
      <div class="landing-cw__stage">
        <div class="landing-cw__light" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="landing-cw__beam landing-cw__beam--l"></span>
            <span class="landing-cw__beam landing-cw__beam--c"></span>
            <span class="landing-cw__beam landing-cw__beam--r"></span>
            <span class="landing-cw__floor"></span>
        </div>

        <header class="landing-cw__head">
            <p class="landing-eyebrow landing-cw__eyebrow">Flagship app · Colorways</p>
            <h2 class="landing-cw__title">One calendar. Every brand.</h2>
            <p class="landing-cw__desc">
                Themed by the same design tokens the whole platform ships.
                Change the colorway; every surface follows.
            </p>
        </header>

        @* The performer: an app vignette under the light. The brand mark
           sits where traffic-light dots would have been (identity rule). *@
        <div class="landing-cw__app" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="landing-cw__appbar">
                <span class="landing-cw__mark">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="16" height="16">
                        <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="15" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.15"/>
                        <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.3"/>
                        <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="5"  fill="currentColor"/>
                    </svg>
                </span>
                <span class="landing-cw__apptitle">Alectrone Calendar</span>
                <span class="landing-cw__pill">Booking</span>
            </div>
            <div class="landing-cw__body">
                <div class="landing-cw__month">
                    <span class="landing-cw__mlabel">@_cwMonthLabel</span>
                    <div class="landing-cw__mgrid">
                        @foreach (var dow in new[] { "M", "T", "W", "T", "F", "S", "S" })
                        {
                            <span class="landing-cw__dow">@dow</span>
                        }
                        @for (var d = 1; d <= 28; d++)
                        {
                            <span class="landing-cw__cell @(d == _cwDay ? "landing-cw__cell--today" : null) @(_cwDotDays.Contains(d) ? "landing-cw__cell--dot" : null)">@d</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-cw__daypanel">
                    <span class="landing-cw__dlabel">@_cwDayLabel</span>
                    <span class="landing-cw__slot landing-cw__slot--active">Design sync · 09:00</span>
                    <span class="landing-cw__slot">Customer demo · 11:30</span>
                    <span class="landing-cw__slot">Roadmap · 14:00</span>
                    <span class="landing-cw__book">Book a slot</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* Swatches are real controls: scroll demonstrates, click pins. *@
        <div class="landing-cw__bar">
            <div class="landing-cw__swatches">
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--iris" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Iris Purple colorway"></button>
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--ruby" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Ruby Red colorway"></button>
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--ember" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Ember Orange colorway"></button>
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--solar" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Solar Amber colorway"></button>
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--meadow" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Meadow Green colorway"></button>
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--aurora" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Aurora Cyan colorway"></button>
                <button type="button" class="landing-cw__swatch landing-cw__swatch--cobalt" data-cw-swatch aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Cobalt Blue colorway"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="landing-cw__captions">
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--0"><b>Iris Purple</b><i>The signature. Alectrona's iris, lit from within.</i></span>
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--1"><b>Ruby Red</b><i>Launch-week urgency, bottled.</i></span>
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--2"><b>Ember Orange</b><i>Warm momentum for the afternoon push.</i></span>
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--3"><b>Solar Amber</b><i>Golden hour for teams that ship at dusk.</i></span>
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--4"><b>Meadow Green</b><i>Fresh starts and clean calendars.</i></span>
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--5"><b>Aurora Cyan</b><i>Cool morning light for calm, early schedules.</i></span>
                <span class="landing-cw__cap landing-cw__cap--6"><b>Cobalt Blue</b><i>Steady blue for the long quarters.</i></span>
            </div>
            <a href="#ai" class="landing__btn landing__btn--outline landing-cw__cta">What else it does</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    @* ══ Scene 6a · SHAPES: the two account shapes, named. It sits after the
         colorway theatre and before the AI scene, so it lands once the visitor
         has seen the calendar, the views and the booking page: by here "the
         same calendar, the same booking pages, the same seven views" refers to
         things already on screen. A pinned runway
         (T2) whose instrument is a SEAT RULE, because the seat count is the
         real difference between the lanes (CalendarPlans.PlanLane): Personal
         is a single point at one seat, Workspace is the span that follows, up
         to the 300-seat ceiling. The personal bank is already lit when the
         scene arrives (those capabilities are already yours); the workspace
         bank rises into the field word by word as the reader travels the
         span, because that is precisely what an organization adds.

         Content rule: every word in the two fields is a ticked row of the
         plan comparison matrix (WelcomePage._compareSections, in CalendarPlans
         order) or a fact on the plan record itself. A word sits on the
         Personal side only if Free or Individual carries it; it sits on the
         Workspace side only if both personal plans lack it and the business
         lane has it. So this scene cannot promise what the tiers do not. ══ *@
    <section id="modes" class="landing-modes" data-scene data-pin data-autoplay="5000" data-chapter="modes"
             aria-label="Personal and Workspace accounts">
        <div class="landing-modes__stage">
            <div class="landing-modes__dawn" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="landing-modes__inner">
                @* Editorial split, the hero's idiom: the statement holds the left
                   column and the qualification sits at its baseline on the right,
                   so the top band is composed rather than half empty. *@
                <header class="landing-modes__head">
                    <div class="landing-modes__head-lead">
                        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Account shapes</p>
                        <h2 class="landing-modes__title">
                            Personal, or <span class="landing-accent">Workspace.</span>
                        </h2>
                    </div>
                    <p class="landing-modes__desc">
                        The product does not change when the team arrives: the same
                        calendar, the same booking pages, the same seven views. What
                        changes is how many people are on it, and whether there is
                        anything to administer.
                    </p>
                </header>

                @* The instrument. Decorative: every fact it draws is written in
                   the plate copy below it, so nothing is lost to assistive tech. *@
                <div class="landing-modes__rule" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="landing-modes__rule-unit">Seats</span>
                    <span class="landing-modes__rule-line"></span>
                    <span class="landing-modes__rule-span"></span>
                    @for (var seats = 0; seats <= SeatCeiling; seats += 10)
                    {
                        var s = seats == 0 ? 1 : seats;
                        var major = s is 1 or 100 or 200 or SeatCeiling;
                        var x = ((s - 1) / (double)(SeatCeiling - 1) * 100.0)
                            .ToString("0.##", Inv);
                        <span class="landing-modes__tick @(major ? "landing-modes__tick--major" : null)" style="--x:@x">
                            @if (major)
                            {
                                <i class="landing-modes__tick-n">@s</i>
                            }
                        </span>
                    }
                    <span class="landing-modes__node"></span>
                    <span class="landing-modes__reader"></span>
                </div>

                <div class="landing-modes__banks">
                    <div class="landing-modes__bank landing-modes__bank--personal">
                        <div class="landing-modes__plate">
                            <span class="landing-modes__plate-ix">01</span>
                            <h3 class="landing-modes__plate-name">Personal</h3>
                            <p class="landing-modes__plate-seats">One seat</p>
                            <p class="landing-modes__plate-line">
                                Your own calendar, billed flat or not at all. No members,
                                no roles, nothing to administer.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <ul class="landing-modes__field">
                            @for (var i = 0; i < _personalWords.Length; i++)
                            {
                                var w = _personalWords[i];
                                <li class="landing-modes__word @(w.Lead ? "landing-modes__word--lead" : null)"
                                    style="--x:@w.X;--y:@w.Y;--i:@i">@w.Text</li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="landing-modes__bank landing-modes__bank--work">
                        <div class="landing-modes__plate">
                            <span class="landing-modes__plate-ix">02</span>
                            <h3 class="landing-modes__plate-name">Workspace</h3>
                            <p class="landing-modes__plate-seats">Two to @SeatCeiling seats</p>
                            <p class="landing-modes__plate-line">
                                @* Not "everything on the left": the banks stack below the
                                   pin breakpoint, so this names the other shape rather
                                   than pointing at where it happens to sit. *@
                                Everything a personal account has, plus the people layer:
                                the admin console at /admin, and per-user billing that
                                only starts once a second person exists.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <ul class="landing-modes__field">
                            @for (var i = 0; i < _workspaceWords.Length; i++)
                            {
                                var w = _workspaceWords[i];
                                <li class="landing-modes__word @(w.Lead ? "landing-modes__word--lead" : null)"
                                    style="--x:@w.X;--y:@w.Y;--i:@i">@w.Text</li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ══ Scene 6b · AI: a pinned runway (T2), in the same height family as
         its neighbours. Scroll IS the assistant. The runway holds at both
         ends - the slight stop a pin buys - and plays four acts between
         them: the sentence writes itself, it resolves into event fields,
         the provider chain answers, the week is read for conflicts, and the
         event lands on the hour that was clear. Every beat is scrubbed from
         --p, so scrolling back plays it in reverse; base, mobile and reduced
         motion render the composed result with no runway at all. ══ *@
    <section id="ai" class="landing-ai" data-scene data-pin data-autoplay="6500" data-chapter="ai" aria-label="AI assistant">
      <div class="landing-ai__stage">
        <div class="landing-ai__dawn" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <div class="landing-ai__inner">
            <div class="landing-ai__copy">
                <p class="landing-eyebrow">AI assistant</p>
                <h2 class="landing-ai__title">Say it. <span class="landing-accent">It's scheduled.</span></h2>
                <p class="landing-ai__desc">
                    Write the sentence you would have said out loud. The assistant
                    reads it as an event, checks it against every calendar you have
                    joined, and books the hour once it knows the hour is clear.
                </p>

                @* The failover claim, drawn. The nodes are deliberately
                   unlabelled: the order is configuration (FallbackOptions
                   .ProviderOrder), so no named provider is depicted as the one
                   that went quiet. *@
                <div class="landing-ai__chain" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="landing-ai__chain-track"></span>
                    <span class="landing-ai__chain-live"></span>
                    @for (var n = 0; n < 5; n++)
                    {
                        var role = n switch { 0 => " landing-ai__node--skip", 1 => " landing-ai__node--ans", _ => "" };
                        <span class="landing-ai__node@(role)" style="--i:@n"></span>
                    }
                </div>
                <p class="landing-ai__chain-note">
                    Five providers stand behind the assistant: Claude, Gemini, Groq,
                    Mistral and OpenRouter. The request takes the first one that
                    answers, so a provider going quiet is a detour, not an outage.
                </p>
            </div>

            @* The instrument. Decorative: every fact it draws is stated in the
               copy beside it, so nothing is lost to assistive tech. *@
            <div class="landing-ai__console" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="landing-ai__bar">
                    <span class="landing-ai__mark">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="18" height="18">
                            <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="15" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)" opacity="0.15"/>
                            <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="10" fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)" opacity="0.3"/>
                            <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="5"  fill="hsl(268, 62%, 58%)"/>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <span class="landing-ai__typewrap">
                        <span class="landing-ai__type">Lunch with Maya on Friday at noon</span>
                    </span>
                </div>

                <ul class="landing-ai__fields">
                    @for (var f = 0; f < _aiFields.Length; f++)
                    {
                        <li class="landing-ai__field" style="--i:@f">
                            <span class="landing-ai__field-k">@_aiFields[f].Key</span>
                            <span class="landing-ai__field-v">@_aiFields[f].Value</span>
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>

                <div class="landing-ai__week">
                    <div class="landing-ai__weekhead">
                        @for (var d = 0; d < _aiDays.Length; d++)
                        {
                            <span class="landing-ai__daylabel @(d == AiHitDay ? "landing-ai__daylabel--hit" : null)">@_aiDays[d]</span>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="landing-ai__hours">
                        @foreach (var mark in _aiHourMarks)
                        {
                            <span class="landing-ai__hour" style="--y:@AiAt(mark)">@AiClock(mark)</span>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="landing-ai__cols">
                        <span class="landing-ai__rules"></span>
                        @for (var d = 0; d < _aiWeek.Length; d++)
                        {
                            <div class="landing-ai__col" style="--i:@d">
                                @foreach (var b in _aiWeek[d])
                                {
                                    <span class="landing-ai__busy"
                                          style="--t:@AiAt(b.Start);--h:@AiSpan(b.Start, b.End)"></span>
                                }
                                @if (d == AiHitDay)
                                {
                                    <span class="landing-ai__drop" style="--t:@AiAt(AiHitStart)"></span>
                                    <span class="landing-ai__free"
                                          style="--t:@AiAt(AiHitStart);--h:@AiSpan(AiHitStart, AiHitEnd)">Free</span>
                                    <span class="landing-ai__chip"
                                          style="--t:@AiAt(AiHitStart);--h:@AiSpan(AiHitStart, AiHitEnd)">
                                        <span class="landing-ai__chip-title">Lunch with Maya</span>
                                        <span class="landing-ai__chip-time">12:00 - 13:00</span>
                                    </span>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                        <span class="landing-ai__scan"></span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p class="landing-ai__confirm">
                    <span class="landing-ai__confirm-check">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
                    </span>
                    On your calendar · Friday 12:00 · no conflicts
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    @* ══ Scene 7 · PROOF: pinned overture (T2/T15/T17). Dawn rises with
         scroll, a billboard numeral anchors the stage, counters earn the
         numbers as the visitor arrives. Every number is counted in this
         repository; adoption statistics are banned until measured. ══ *@
    <section class="landing-proof" data-pin data-autoplay="4500" data-chapter="proof" aria-label="Product facts">
        <div class="landing-proof__stage">
            <div class="landing-proof__dawn" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <span class="landing-proof__billboard" aria-hidden="true">256</span>
            <h2 class="landing-proof__statement">Built to be trusted with everyone's time.</h2>
            <p class="landing-proof__note">No adoption theatre. These are engineering facts, counted in the product.</p>
            <dl class="landing-proof__stats">
                <div class="landing-proof__stat">
                    <dt class="landing-proof__num" data-count-to="7">7</dt>
                    <dd class="landing-proof__label">Calendar views, day through timeline</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-proof__stat">
                    <dt class="landing-proof__num" data-count-to="11">11</dt>
                    <dd class="landing-proof__label">Scoped permissions over calendars, events, and bookings</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-proof__stat">
                    <dt class="landing-proof__num" data-count-to="256">256</dt>
                    <dd class="landing-proof__label">Bits of AES-GCM on every encrypted field</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="landing-proof__stat">
                    <dt class="landing-proof__num" data-count-to="5">5</dt>
                    <dd class="landing-proof__label">AI providers behind one assistant</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* Scene 8 (PRICING) is deliberately absent here: no plan catalog ships with
       the demo and it quotes no price, so the nav item, the chapter-rail stop and
       the footer link went with it. Nothing replaces it - the film runs straight
       from Proof into the close. *@

    @* ══ Scene 10 · Close: the encore. The demo keeps the encore composition but
         not its plan names, so no pricing detail survives here. ══ *@
    <section class="landing-close" data-scene>
        <div class="landing-close__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="landing__section-inner">
            <h2 class="landing-close__title">Ready to own the week?</h2>
            <p class="landing-close__subtitle">
                Team scheduling, public booking pages, and an assistant that
